# Lab proof

## Program
File: homeguard_system.ipynb

## How to run
Run command: Run All in VS Code's notebook

## How the code works
The code uses lists, dictionaries, cases, functions and conditions to read motion, temperature, door, and smoke sensors. It evaluates each reading against parameters such as safety, security, comfort rules for the selected system mode (away, home, sleep) and generates alerts with various degrees of priorities when the conditions are met. It displays the alerts, and logs with timestamps.


## Fixed test cases and output

### Test 1: SECURITY TEST (open door)
Input: Door Open in Away mode
Output:
[ALERT!] 🚨 HIGH: Door opened while away!

### Test 2a: SAFETY TEST (temperature)
Input: 30°F in HOME mode; this is below the 35°F safety limit.
Output:
[ALERT!] ⚠️ MEDIUM: Abnormal temperature reading: 30°F
[ALERT!] ℹ️ LOW: Temperature outside comfort range: 30°F

###Test 2b: SAFETY TEST (smoke)
Input: Smoke detected in Home mode
Output:
[ALERT!] 🚨 HIGH: Smoke detected!

###Test 3: COMFORT TEST
Input: temperature of 60°F in HOME mode, which is below the comfort range of 65-75°F
Output:
[ALERT!] ℹ️ LOW: Temperature outside comfort range: 60°F

